+      <p>This section explains how KEYCON accesses, uses, stores, protects, shares and deletes the data it receives from your Google account.</p>
+      <p>Data accessed. When you sign in with Google, we receive your name, email address and profile picture (basic profile). If you grant permission, we also receive access to the calendar.events scope, which lets KEYCON create events in your Google Calendar. We do not access your Gmail, contacts, Google Drive or any other data in your Google account, and we do not read the events already in your calendar.</p>
+      <p>How we use it. Your name, email address and profile picture are used only to create and identify your KEYCON account and to show your profile in the app. Calendar access is used only to create, when you ask, the appointments you schedule in KEYCON as events in your Google Calendar with a Google Meet link, and to show you that link. We use Google user data only to provide and improve these user-facing features.</p>
+      <p>Sharing. We do not sell Google user data. We do not share, transfer or disclose it to third parties, except: (a) to our infrastructure provider (Supabase, which hosts authentication and the database), which processes it on our behalf only to operate the service; (b) when required by law or court order; or (c) with your consent. We do not use or transfer this data for advertising (targeted, personalized, retargeted or interest-based), for data brokers or information resellers, for credit-worthiness or lending purposes, or to create databases.</p>
+      <p>Artificial intelligence. We do not use Google user data, including data obtained through Google Workspace APIs, to develop, improve or train generalized or non-personalized artificial intelligence or machine learning models. KEYCON’s AI reply feature does not receive Google user data.</p>
+      <p>Storage and protection. Your name, email address and profile picture are stored in your account in our database (Supabase), encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS) and at rest, with access restricted to your own account. Google access and refresh tokens are stored only on your device; to renew access, the refresh token is sent over an encrypted connection to a secure server function that exchanges it with Google and does not store it. Events are created directly in your Google Calendar; we do not keep a copy of your calendar.</p>
+      <p>Retention and deletion. We keep your name, email address and profile picture while your account exists. You can request deletion of your account and this data at keyconapp.com/excluir-conta.html or by email at contact@keyconapp.com; we complete it within 30 days. Google tokens are deleted from your device when you sign out or uninstall the app. You can remove KEYCON’s access to your Google account at any time at myaccount.google.com/permissions; after that we can no longer access your calendar. Events already created stay in your Google Calendar until you delete them.</p>
+      <p>Limited Use. KEYCON’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy (developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy), including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
